{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-opg-2242-goldberg-s-conjecture-49d583ed-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T15:37:58Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-opg-2242-goldberg-s-conjecture-49d583ed-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-opg-2242-goldberg-s-conjecture-49d583ed-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-2242-goldberg-s-conjecture-49d583ed-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-2242"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "The overfull parameter is defined as follows: $$ w(G) = \\max_{H \\subseteq G} \\left\\lceil \\frac{ |E(H)| }{ \\lfloor \\tfrac{1}{2} |V(H)| \\rfloor} \\right\\rceil. $$ Conjecture Every graph $G$ satisfies $\\chi'(G) \\le \\max\\{ \\Delta(G) + 1, w(G) \\}$."}, "statement_sha256": "8ef6b3426557526ac8284f9417606536184750e1abadeba528c446816f14d661"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-2242-goldberg-s-conjecture-49d583ed-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-2242"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha256": "781c706ebf4db8dc4f5007488546461d4fdd1abc6cfeb32a73aecad337e95262", "problem_id": "problem:um-opg-2242-goldberg-s-conjecture-49d583ed", "root_obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-